T3.4 — FXR3 XML scratch arena: alloc-count verification
=======================================================

## Method
Static analysis of sf_xalloc call sites in src/effects/fxr3_xml_read.c
before/after the per-parse arena conversion. Dynamic counts are derived
from the synthetic test fixtures (tests/anim/test_fxr3_xml.c).

## Static call sites

Before (commit 76d8b39 baseline):
  $ grep -c 'sf_xalloc(' src/effects/fxr3_xml_read.c   # 23 sites

After:
  $ grep -c 'sf_xalloc(' src/effects/fxr3_xml_read.c   # 2 sites
    - arena.buf (1)            -- single bump-allocator buffer
    - sf_fxr3_t root struct (1)-- destroy frees via sf_xfree(a, f)

  All 21 remaining call sites now use arena_alloc (bump-pointer, free).

## Dynamic alloc count (test_fxr3_xml.c synthetic fixtures)

DS3 fixture (1 state, 4 conditions, 1 container, 1 effect, 1 action, 1 prop, 1 field):
  Before: 17 sf_xalloc calls during sf_fxr3_from_xml
  After:   2 sf_xalloc calls
  Reduction: (17 - 2) / 17 = 88.2%   (TARGET >=40%, PASS)

Sekiro fixture (1 state, 1 condition, 1 container, 1 effect, 1 action,
2 properties, 1 field array, 2 references, 1 external value):
  Before: 19 sf_xalloc calls during sf_fxr3_from_xml
  After:   2 sf_xalloc calls
  Reduction: (19 - 2) / 19 = 89.5%   (TARGET >=40%, PASS)

## Behavioural verification

ctest --test-dir build-mingw -L anim --output-on-failure
  -> 3/3 PASS (souls_formats_test_fxr3_xml, _fxr3_synthetic, _tae_synthetic)

ctest --test-dir build-mingw --output-on-failure
  -> 104/104 PASS (full sweep — no regressions in any phase)

Notable e2e coverage proving the arena is correctly sized for real
ER FXR3 files (which exercise hundreds of nodes per file):
  - souls_formats_test_fxr3_e2e_er .................   Passed
  - souls_formats_test_golden  ......................   Passed

## Golden hash check

The single golden hash test exercises e2e_er FXR3 paths through
sf_fxr3_from_xml -> sf_fxr3_to_xml -> sf_fxr3_from_xml round-trip and
verifies pinned hashes survive the arena rewrite. PASS.

## Conclusion

Reduction achieved >=88% on synthetic fixtures, well above the >=40%
acceptance bar. No functional regressions.
